--- Mutant J : byte-taking entry point, no decode, guard goes LIVE ----------- FINDING 1
    func ValidateSortedNames(raw [][]byte) error {
        values := make([]any, 0, len(raw))
        for _, item := range raw {
            values = append(values, string(item))   // bytes -> Go value, no decodeStrict
        }
        return validateSortedUniqueStrings(values, "names")
    }
RESULT: SURVIVES EVERYTHING
    P1 PASS   P2 PASS (still reports 7/7)   P3 PASS   P4 PASS
    go test ./internal/canonicaljson/ -count=1  ->  ok  18.491s
Probe driven through the exported entry point proves the "subsumed" guard is the term that refuses:
    ValidateSortedNames([][]byte{{0xff, 0xfe}})
    -> invalid canonical object identity: member names[0] must be a UTF-8 string
byteInputParameters checks parameter SHAPE, not that the bytes reach decodeStrict, and a
[]byte -> string conversion is not a JSON decode, so neither half of the pin sees it.
Not one of the three disclosed unmodelled constructions.

