RESULT: SURVIVES EVERYTHING
    P4 PASS  ("--- PASS: TestDecodeStrictIsTheOnlyJSONDecodeInTheProductionPackage")
    go test ./internal/canonicaljson/ -count=1  ->  ok  17.785s
P4 matches selector.X only when the identifier is literally "json"; it resolves no import path.
Same hole admits any decoder from a different package (encoding/json/v2, third-party).
README claim "Adding a second decoder reddens the pin" does not reproduce.

--- Mutant M : new undocumented re-check written as utf8.Valid -------------- FINDING 3
Added to closed_shapes.go:
    func reviewMutantCheck(text string) error {
        if !utf8.Valid([]byte(text)) { return invalidIdentity("mutant re-check") }
        return nil
    }
RESULT: SURVIVES — P1 PASS  P2 PASS  P3 PASS
utf8GuardedFunctions and P3 key on ValidString with the package identifier spelled "utf8".
utf8.Valid is an idiom already used in this package (decodeStrict, canonical.go:328), so a
re-check written that way silently joins the undocumented survivors. Contradicts the comment at
utf8_subsumption_test.go:106 ("a new re-check is covered by this pin the moment it is written").

